// Title: Suspicious MSExchangeMailboxReplication ASPX Write
// Sigma ID: 7280c9f3-a5af-45d0-916a-bc01cb4151c9
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-02-25 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: initial-access, T1190, persistence, T1505.003
// Description: Detects suspicious activity in which the MSExchangeMailboxReplication process writes .asp and
//   .apsx files to disk, which could be a sign of ProxyShell exploitation
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://redcanary.com/blog/blackbyte-ransomware/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_susp_exchange_aspx_write.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\MSExchangeMailboxReplication.exe" and (FolderPath endswith ".aspx" or FolderPath endswith ".asp")
